1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,280
Last time, we found magnets hiding at home: in the fridge door,

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:06,290
the whiteboard, and the doorstop.

3
00:00:08,887 --> 00:00:10,537
A magnetic fishing game!

4
00:00:10,647 --> 00:00:14,017
The rod has a magnet, and every fish has a steel clip.

5
00:00:14,442 --> 00:00:17,342
A little water strider is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:17,602 --> 00:00:18,832
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:19,108 --> 00:00:20,948
Lock in first with your fingers.

8
00:00:21,218 --> 00:00:23,048
One finger for every point.

9
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:25,010
Today you'll learn:

10
00:00:25,214 --> 00:00:26,724
Cranes and trains.

11
00:00:27,001 --> 00:00:28,711
Magnets in hospitals.

12
00:00:28,982 --> 00:00:30,632
Design a magnet toy.

13
00:00:32,328 --> 00:00:33,208
Round one.

14
00:00:33,538 --> 00:00:37,458
Basil swaps every steel clip on the fish for an aluminium clip.

15
00:00:37,728 --> 00:00:38,938
What happens now?

16
00:00:39,228 --> 00:00:41,278
One, the fish are caught as before.

17
00:00:41,558 --> 00:00:43,338
Two, no fish can be caught.

18
00:00:43,618 --> 00:00:46,098
Three, the fish are pushed away from the rod.

19
00:00:46,388 --> 00:00:47,748
Show me your fingers.

20
00:00:53,272 --> 00:00:54,252
Locked in!

21
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:55,150
One!

22
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:56,460
A clip is a clip.

23
00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:57,840
I will catch them all!

24
00:00:58,192 --> 00:00:58,982
Two.

25
00:00:59,192 --> 00:01:02,022
Aluminium is not a magnetic material.

26
00:01:02,372 --> 00:01:05,572
Two. And the magnet will not push them away either.

27
00:01:05,692 --> 00:01:07,172
It just does nothing.

28
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:09,060
The answer is two!

29
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,900
Did you show two fingers?

30
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:12,580
Put one finger up!

31
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:16,170
A magnet does not attract aluminium, and it does not push it

32
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:16,840
away.

33
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:19,410
With steel clips, the game works again!

34
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,810
Why does a scrapyard crane use an electromagnet?

35
00:01:22,990 --> 00:01:24,790
Why not a big normal magnet?

36
00:01:25,666 --> 00:01:26,816
Look closer.

37
00:01:27,406 --> 00:01:31,276
Switch the crane's disc on, and it attracts the iron and steel.

38
00:01:31,846 --> 00:01:34,446
The wood and the plastic stay behind.

39
00:01:34,718 --> 00:01:37,248
Swing it over the lorry, and switch it off.

40
00:01:37,818 --> 00:01:39,138
The scrap drops.

41
00:01:39,708 --> 00:01:42,148
A normal magnet could never let go!

42
00:01:45,147 --> 00:01:46,447
Say it with me!

43
00:01:47,158 --> 00:01:51,828
The crane has a large iron disc that becomes a powerful electromagnet.

44
00:01:52,318 --> 00:01:56,428
The electromagnet then attracts objects made of iron and steel.

45
00:01:59,902 --> 00:02:00,802
Showdown!

46
00:02:01,112 --> 00:02:02,242
Double points.

47
00:02:02,512 --> 00:02:05,052
Momo's toy design has one mistake.

48
00:02:05,332 --> 00:02:07,112
Line one, two, or three?

49
00:02:07,402 --> 00:02:08,872
Show me with your fingers.

50
00:02:09,008 --> 00:02:11,418
One: tape a bar magnet on a toy car.

51
00:02:11,678 --> 00:02:14,208
Two: hold another bar magnet behind it.

52
00:02:14,288 --> 00:02:17,038
Three: to push the car away, face a North pole to a

53
00:02:17,058 --> 00:02:18,078
South pole.

54
00:02:24,818 --> 00:02:25,798
Locked in!

55
00:02:26,076 --> 00:02:26,806
Three!

56
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:29,106
A North pole and a South pole attract.

57
00:02:29,186 --> 00:02:31,916
To push the car, face two North poles together.

58
00:02:32,116 --> 00:02:33,426
Like poles repel!

59
00:02:34,405 --> 00:02:35,495
Three fingers?

60
00:02:35,735 --> 00:02:37,665
Put up two more on your score hand!

61
00:02:38,165 --> 00:02:39,515
Be a floating train!

62
00:02:39,795 --> 00:02:40,775
Shrink down.

63
00:02:41,055 --> 00:02:41,985
Quietly.

64
00:02:44,274 --> 00:02:47,284
You are a train, floating a little above your track.

65
00:02:48,064 --> 00:02:51,194
There are magnets on you, and magnets on the track.

66
00:02:51,778 --> 00:02:54,498
They push away from each other, and hold you up.

67
00:02:55,288 --> 00:02:57,068
Nothing rubs on the track.

68
00:02:57,649 --> 00:03:00,239
So you glide, smooth and very fast!

69
00:03:02,179 --> 00:03:04,439
So magnets can push a whole train up?

70
00:03:05,316 --> 00:03:06,466
Look closer.

71
00:03:07,046 --> 00:03:10,436
In this maglev train, the magnets on the train and on the

72
00:03:10,456 --> 00:03:12,346
track push each other away.

73
00:03:12,916 --> 00:03:15,696
The train floats, so it can go very fast.

74
00:03:15,981 --> 00:03:18,921
A maglev train is a train that floats above its track on

75
00:03:18,941 --> 00:03:21,801
magnets, such as this train in my video!

76
00:03:22,528 --> 00:03:25,538
In a hospital, there is a giant magnet too.

77
00:03:26,118 --> 00:03:28,818
It takes pictures of the inside of the body.

78
00:03:29,092 --> 00:03:31,672
MRI is a safe and painless test.

79
00:03:32,817 --> 00:03:36,367
An MRI scanner is a large round magnet with a tunnel in

80
00:03:36,387 --> 00:03:40,227
the centre, that takes pictures of the inside of the body!

81
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:44,753
Say it with me!

82
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:48,720
The magnets on the train and the tracks repel one another.

83
00:03:51,351 --> 00:03:55,001
Magnets can attract other magnets or magnetic objects.

84
00:03:55,251 --> 00:03:57,451
Magnets can also repel each other.

85
00:03:57,711 --> 00:04:01,601
When this happens, the magnets are interacting with one another or other

86
00:04:01,621 --> 00:04:02,511
objects.

87
00:04:03,097 --> 00:04:06,977
Interacting means acting on each other, such as two magnets pulling or

88
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:08,287
pushing each other!

89
00:04:09,149 --> 00:04:10,253
Say it with us!

90
00:04:10,913 --> 00:04:12,118
The fridge door?

91
00:04:12,493 --> 00:04:13,846
A magnetic strip!

92
00:04:17,313 --> 00:04:18,270
The crane?

93
00:04:18,893 --> 00:04:20,392
An electromagnet!

94
00:04:23,713 --> 00:04:24,960
The floating train?

95
00:04:25,293 --> 00:04:26,788
Magnets that repel!

96
00:04:30,968 --> 00:04:32,428
Show me your score hand!

97
00:04:32,708 --> 00:04:34,158
Two fingers or more?

98
00:04:34,448 --> 00:04:35,808
You beat the Buddies.

99
00:04:36,098 --> 00:04:37,168
Three fingers?

100
00:04:37,448 --> 00:04:38,448
High five!

101
00:04:38,876 --> 00:04:40,596
Did you spot the water strider?

102
00:04:40,886 --> 00:04:42,576
It was by the stepping stone!

103
00:04:42,855 --> 00:04:44,165
Here is a fun fact!

104
00:04:44,235 --> 00:04:47,175
A water strider stands on water and does not sink.

105
00:04:47,375 --> 00:04:49,585
Tiny hairs on its legs keep them dry.

106
00:04:49,795 --> 00:04:52,695
It floats like our train, with no magnets at all!

107
00:04:52,899 --> 00:04:54,179
Tell someone at home!

108
00:04:54,758 --> 00:04:59,008
Properties of magnets allow us to use magnets in everyday life.

109
00:04:59,804 --> 00:05:03,594
And that is the end of our Primary Three science adventures!

110
00:05:03,874 --> 00:05:07,304
Thank you for playing with Pip, Basil and Momo all year.

111
00:05:07,729 --> 00:05:10,739
Count the magnets in your home today, and tell someone how many

112
00:05:10,759 --> 00:05:11,769
you found!

113
00:05:12,492 --> 00:05:14,692
Let's read today's key words together!

114
00:05:14,982 --> 00:05:15,742
Ready?

115
00:05:16,029 --> 00:05:17,239
Maglev train.

116
00:05:18,957 --> 00:05:20,207
MRI scanner.

117
00:05:21,996 --> 00:05:23,046
Interacting.

118
00:05:24,691 --> 00:05:25,631
Well done!

119
00:05:26,613 --> 00:05:27,714
Say it with us!

120
00:05:28,514 --> 00:05:29,264
Ready?

121
00:05:29,387 --> 00:05:30,047
One!

122
00:05:30,387 --> 00:05:31,087
two!

123
00:05:31,392 --> 00:05:32,567
Now you know!
